<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/</link><lastBuildDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:35:24 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Middle East</category><title>US journalist injured during Israeli settler attack on West Bank olive harvest</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261016-us-journalist-injured-during-israeli-settler-attack-on-west-bank-olive-harvest</link><description>
About 80 Israeli settlers set fire to olive trees and threw stones at Palestinians in a West Bank village Friday, injuring at least two people, including a US photojournalist with The Washington Post. The coordinated attack came as violence by settlers is on the rise during the olive harvest in the occupied Palestinian territory.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/03083cb6-c96d-11f1-8513-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3GA69H.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/03083cb6-c96d-11f1-8513-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3GA69H.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">89f613f2-c96c-11f1-b53b-a3afa13a0591</guid><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 15:01:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/03083cb6-c96d-11f1-8513-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3GA69H.jpg">© Ahmad Gharabli, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Saudi Arabia postpones major sporting events amid Houthi attacks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/saudi-arabia-postpones-major-sporting-events-amid-houthi-attacks</link><description>
Several major sporting events in Saudi Arabia have been cancelled or postponed as a result of repeated deadly attacks from Iran-backed Houthi rebels against the Kingdom's airports and infrastructure. FRANCE 24's Mark Owen speaks with Guy Barton, Visiting Fellow at Lancaster University and co-creator and co-host of The FootPol Podcast.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/da51f614-c8d5-11f1-aa87-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-213110-214026-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/da51f614-c8d5-11f1-aa87-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-213110-214026-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dfe2d774-c8d5-11f1-84a0-ebd1ed049b0f</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:31:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Houthi attack on palace used by Yemen government in Aden kills five</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261015-houthi-attack-on-palace-used-by-yemen-government-in-aden-kills-five</link><description>
At least five people were killed and 16 wounded Thursday in a Houthi missile and drone attack on the palace located in Yemen's interim capital – the southern port city of Aden, used by the country's internationally recognised government, an official said.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/726e8c4a-c8c3-11f1-b18b-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-15T171257Z-1450446933-RC2N3OAX74ZS-RTRMADP-3-SAUDI-YEMEN-ADEN-BOOMS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/726e8c4a-c8c3-11f1-b18b-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-15T171257Z-1450446933-RC2N3OAX74ZS-RTRMADP-3-SAUDI-YEMEN-ADEN-BOOMS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">27f1fba8-c8cc-11f1-b6d1-f56d77e2991f</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:57:48 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/726e8c4a-c8c3-11f1-b18b-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-15T171257Z-1450446933-RC2N3OAX74ZS-RTRMADP-3-SAUDI-YEMEN-ADEN-BOOMS.jpg">© Social media via Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Tête à tête</category><title>Election delay 'a terrible disappointment', Palestinian activist Samer Sinijlawi says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261015-election-delay-a-terrible-disappointment-palestinian-activist-samer-sinijlawi-says</link><description>
In an interview with FRANCE 24, Palestinian activist Samer Sinijlawi called the postponement of the first legislative elections in 20 years to September 2027 "a terrible disappointment" for a generation that has never had a chance to vote. He also dismissed the citing of Israeli restrictions as an excuse, pointing instead to a "rejection" of change among ageing Palestinian leaders.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/062cef5e-c89b-11f1-9274-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-PKG-CLEAN-TETE-A-TETE-SAMER-SINIJLAWI-AUBIN-Sophian.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/062cef5e-c89b-11f1-9274-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-PKG-CLEAN-TETE-A-TETE-SAMER-SINIJLAWI-AUBIN-Sophian.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fa9785f0-c877-11f1-b167-2f6a248273a3</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:17:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marc PERELMAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Perspective</category><title>War escalates between Houthis and Riyadh: How did we get here?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261015-war-escalates-between-houthis-and-riyadh-how-did-we-get-here</link><description>
To discuss the ongoing conflict between the Houthi rebels and the Saudi-backed coalition, we speak to Jules Grange Gastinel, a researcher at France's CNRS research body specialising in the Houthi movement. He tells us why the conflict has escalated and what the Houthis want.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dee9186e-c89f-11f1-9be4-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-a8242456.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dee9186e-c89f-11f1-9be4-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-a8242456.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6ed87506-c87c-11f1-98a8-af119fcfe771</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:16:57 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Oliver FARRY</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Houthis deny targeting holy city of Medina after Saudi Arabia says it intercepted missile</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261015-houthis-deny-targeting-holy-city-medina-after-saudi-arabia-says-intercepted-missile</link><description>
Yemen's Houthis denied carrying out an attack on Saudi Arabia on Thursday, shortly after Riyadh said it had intercepted a missile targeting the region around the holy city of Medina. Riyadh also accused Tehran of stoking tensions between the Houthis and government forces in the latest escalation.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/68f50d26-c880-11f1-9523-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/000-1SL9CP.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/68f50d26-c880-11f1-9523-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/000-1SL9CP.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7cce943c-c87d-11f1-8d45-fb20c1b501ef</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:24:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/68f50d26-c880-11f1-9523-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/000-1SL9CP.jpg">© Majed Al-Charfi, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>‘Growing ambitions’: Dr. Kendall on Houthis’ quest to be recognised as Yemen’s ‘legitimate' leaders</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/growing-ambitions-dr-kendall-on-houthis-quest-to-be-recognised-as-yemen-s-legitimate-leaders</link><description>
What is the strategic logic behind the Houthis’ increasingly high-risk confrontation with Saudi Arabia? “Their experience in the past is that threats pay,” explains Dr. Elizabeth Kendall, Middle East specialist and President of Girton College, University of Cambridge. Dr. Kendall argues that the movement’s increasingly audacious military operations are not merely expressions of ideological hostility or Iranian influence, but calculated instruments of political coercion aimed at securing legitimacy, expanding territorial control and strengthening its negotiating leverage.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5f96d39c-c7ed-11f1-b60f-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-161507-162732-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5f96d39c-c7ed-11f1-b60f-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-161507-162732-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">64fb60fa-c7ed-11f1-8501-43b1ddbf6a9e</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:18:04 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Houthis threaten escalation after strike on Saudi oil giant Aramco</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261014-yemen-houthis-vow-continue-saudi-attacks-oil-giant-aramco-headquarters-hit</link><description>
Yemen's Houthi rebels said Wednesday they had targeted facilities belonging to Saudi oil giant Aramco after officials in Riyadh reported a strike on a building in an area housing the energy giant's headquarters. The Iran-back militia also claimed missile strikes on the capital Riyadh and vowed to continue attacking Saudi airports and oil facilities.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84e4ed72-bf65-11f1-8c8d-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D26B6KC.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84e4ed72-bf65-11f1-8c8d-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D26B6KC.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">79def022-c7e3-11f1-a49e-a91b34a35119</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:21:53 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84e4ed72-bf65-11f1-8c8d-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D26B6KC.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Blasts rock Riyadh as Houthis vow to continue striking Saudi airports, oil facilities</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261014-live-saudi-arabia-reports-aramco-building-hit-and-four-wounded-in-houthi-missile-attacks</link><description>
Yemen's Iran-backed Houthis said on Wednesday they had targeted facilities belonging to Saudi oil giant Aramco as well as Riyadh airport after loud blasts rattled the Saudi capital. The Saudi-led coalition fighting the Houthis earlier said it had intercepted a missile fired towards Riyadh. Read about the day’s events as they unfolded on our liveblog. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/569c98ee-c31a-11f1-9635-c55799ef8309/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26276415281654-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/569c98ee-c31a-11f1-9635-c55799ef8309/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26276415281654-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d282ecb4-c780-11f1-b34d-cd2bd25d3254</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 03:39:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/569c98ee-c31a-11f1-9635-c55799ef8309/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26276415281654-1.jpg">© AP file photo</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Oil facility near Yemen capital Sanaa hit by Saudi Arabia, Houthis say</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261013-oil-facility-near-yemen-capital-sanaa-hit-by-saudi-arabia-houthis-say</link><description>
Houthi media reported an ​attack ‌by Saudi Arabia on ⁠the ‌Yemen Oil Company ⁠in Sanaa on Tuesday, which came ‌shortly after the ‌Saudi-led coalition ​ordered the evacuation of the ​facility ​ahead of ​a military ​operation. The Iran-backed rebels had warned that they would target Riyadh's airport and other sites in the country if Saudi Arabia followed through on its threat.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/09974fea-c710-11f1-8feb-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-04T160923Z-192328429-RC2AWNASBLFE-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-YEMEN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/09974fea-c710-11f1-8feb-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-04T160923Z-192328429-RC2AWNASBLFE-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-YEMEN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">aa990e7e-c710-11f1-9026-f5d5f270ea54</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:53:39 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/09974fea-c710-11f1-8feb-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-04T160923Z-192328429-RC2AWNASBLFE-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-YEMEN.jpg">© Stringer, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>French embassy in Riyadh tells citizens to avoid Saudi airports targeted by Houthis</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261013-french-embassy-in-riyadh-tells-citizens-to-avoid-saudi-airports-targeted-by-houthis</link><description>
France's embassy in Saudi Arabia told its citizens to avoid the airports in Riyadh, Jeddah and Dammam on Tuesday as fighting escalates between a Saudi-led coalition and Yemen's Iran-backed Houthi rebels, who have been attacking Saudi airports and oil facilities since last week.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2b3b6f86-c707-11f1-b9b0-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A6JF8WH.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2b3b6f86-c707-11f1-b9b0-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A6JF8WH.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">77d63f76-c70a-11f1-9784-3ffc75c10a41</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:51:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2b3b6f86-c707-11f1-b9b0-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A6JF8WH.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Hope so heavy to carry': Al-Shaer on harrowing plight, emotional toll, struggle to survive in Gaza</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/hope-so-heavy-to-carry-al-shaer-on-harrowing-plight-emotional-toll-struggle-to-survive-in-gaza</link><description>
Eve Irvine is pleased to welcome Palestinian writer and poet Mahmoud Al-Shaer, “Am I real, or just a number in this war?” In I Am Still Alive: Dispatches from Gaza, Palestinian writer Mahmoud Al-Shaer explores how war transforms memory, childhood and the meaning of existence. Recounting his family's displacement, his daughter's understanding of a world reduced to tents, and his evacuation from Gaza, he reflects on writing as an act of resistance against erasure. His testimony reveals how the struggle for survival extends beyond physical destruction to the preservation of identity, collective memory and the possibility of a normal life.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d9397d8a-c603-11f1-9405-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261006-081057-082155-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d9397d8a-c603-11f1-9405-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261006-081057-082155-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">def42f40-c603-11f1-bc89-fb9316923bc6</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:36:15 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Airlines suspend flights to Riyadh amid security fears</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/airlines-suspend-flights-to-riyadh-amid-security-fears</link><description>
Flights to and from Riyadh have been suspended following deadly Houthi attacks, with several international airlines extending cancellations through October 19. The disruption threatens Saudi Arabia’s ambitions to become a major global aviation hub, while Delta has postponed its first direct US flights to the Kingdom until March 2027.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3556cb4-c4d3-11f1-90a7-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/AP314998123886.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3556cb4-c4d3-11f1-90a7-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/AP314998123886.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6271894a-c6e4-11f1-b3d5-d1eabdeaa934</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 09:19:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>No, these pictures do not show the Houthi attacks on Riyadh's King Khalid Airport</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261012-no-these-pictures-do-not-show-the-houthi-attacks-on-riyadh-king-khalid-airport</link><description>
As Saudi Arabia’s King Khalid International Airport suffers a string of deadly attacks, claimed by Yemen's Houthi rebels, a slew of AI-generated or decontextualised videos and photos have been circulating on social media, purporting to show the strikes of the last few days. We take a closer look in Truth or Fake.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dbd3588e-c6e6-11f1-929a-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-1730100666acdf7116f2c37-17236945.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dbd3588e-c6e6-11f1-929a-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-1730100666acdf7116f2c37-17236945.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">caa897fc-c67f-11f1-9dc9-25558f5b53dc</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 20:59:18 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Emerald MAXWELL</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Houthi official warns of 'swift, painful response' if US enters Yemen war</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/houthi-official-warns-of-swift-painful-response-if-us-enters-yemen-war</link><description>
A Houthi official on Monday warned the US it would receive a "painful response" if it entered the war in Yemen, where Saudi Arabia has reportedly requested Washington's help in dealing with the group as it weathers repeated attacks. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b0b3ed52-c66f-11f1-8380-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-203211-203405-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b0b3ed52-c66f-11f1-8380-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-203211-203405-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b6002b5e-c66f-11f1-a4fd-7d546295e59f</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 19:42:01 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Houthis 'are thriving and surviving by creating war', Yemen ambassador says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/houthis-are-thriving-and-surviving-by-creating-war-yemen-ambassador-says</link><description>
Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Yemen's ambassador to France Riyad Yassin Abdallah says that the Iran-backed Houthi "are thriving and surviving by creating war". Saudi Arabia's energy minister on Monday said the country had been tested but would mount a "serious" response after a string of attacks on Riyadh's international airport by Yemen's Houthis that left 18 people dead.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/50966bf2-c66f-11f1-924c-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-203406-204032-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/50966bf2-c66f-11f1-924c-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-203406-204032-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">568bcbec-c66f-11f1-94a0-59d56837f9ff</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 19:08:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>How exposed is Saudi Arabia? Yemen's Houthis scale up drone and missile attacks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261012-how-exposed-is-saudi-arabia-yemen-s-houthis-scale-up-drone-and-missile-attacks</link><description>
How exposed is Saudi Arabia? Just as Iran's retaliation to Donald Trump's war suddenly exposed the vulnerability of neighbouring Gulf states, how much is Riyadh reeling from the escalation with Yemen's Tehran-backed Houthis? We assess the physical and material damage from strikes on airports and oil facilities, as well as eventual repercussions for the kingdom's ability to project strength. In the age of cheap drone warfare, how much can a battle-hardened militia push against the region's richest nation?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c294b8ba-c5ae-11f1-9976-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-11T133451Z-158209492-RC211OAHP5D3-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-AIRPORT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c294b8ba-c5ae-11f1-9976-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-11T133451Z-158209492-RC211OAHP5D3-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-AIRPORT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">539930c8-c665-11f1-9bc2-0933522cf0fa</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:33:12 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Saudi Arabia extends Riyadh aiport suspension, vows deadly response to Houthis strikes</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/saudi-arabia-extends-riyadh-aiport-suspension-vows-deadly-response-to-houthis-strikes</link><description>
Saudi Arabia extended on Monday the closure of the international airport in Riyadh after announcing the Saudi-led coalition was responding to Houthi combined drone and missile attacks. On Saturday, another attack left 13 dead and over 300 injured. This is one of the worst disruptions to Saudi aviation in years – marking a significant escalation in the war with Yemen's Houthi rebels. Details and analysis by FRANCE 24 international affairs editor Philip Turle.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8e087024-c657-11f1-b925-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-170113-170804-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8e087024-c657-11f1-b925-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-170113-170804-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">930a6d16-c657-11f1-ad31-37097af3614a</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:21:57 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Observers</category><title>Concerts of pro-Assad singers cancelled in Syria</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261012-concerts-pro-assad-singers-cancelled</link><description>
The concerts of several singers accused of supporting the regime of deposed president Bashar al-Assad have been cancelled this summer in Syria. People in Homs ripped down posters advertising performances by artists Mohamad Iskandar and Hossam Jneed, denouncing their previous links with the regime. One of the musicians later publicly apologised. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/71e2a3a2-c624-11f1-a2f5-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/vlcsnap-2026-10-12-11h47m40s172.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/71e2a3a2-c624-11f1-a2f5-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/vlcsnap-2026-10-12-11h47m40s172.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c4228538-c624-11f1-a08d-f15a4abace13</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:53:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>The FRANCE 24 Observers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Perspective</category><title>'Perfect Victims' author Mohammed El-Kurd challenges how Palestinian suffering is viewed</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261012-perfect-victims-author-mohammed-el-kurd-challenges-how-palestinian-suffering-is-viewed</link><description>
Mohammed El-Kurd is a Palestinian writer, poet and journalist. He is the author of the poetry collection Rifqa and the book "Perfect Victims and the Politics of Appeal", which was just published in French translation last week. Mohammed grew up in Sheikh Jarrah in East Jerusalem and as a child, his family were displaced from their home by Israeli settlers in a high-profile eviction. He spoke to us in Perspective.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d41606a0-c63c-11f1-ac79-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-18157455296accd9cdf27ba1-37613308.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d41606a0-c63c-11f1-ac79-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-18157455296accd9cdf27ba1-37613308.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">70462e7c-c626-11f1-9854-7b78552cd9fc</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:12:47 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Oliver FARRY</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Netanyahu demands probe into Israeli anonymous whistleblowers in 'NAZA' documentary</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/netanyahu-demands-probe-into-israeli-anonymous-whistleblowers-in-naza-documentary</link><description>
Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu on Sunday called for an investigation into the anonymous sources featured in the award-winning Gaza war documentary "NAZA". The film, which won the Special Jury Prize at the Venice Film Festival last month, is based on testimony from 24 unnamed Israeli military whistleblowers who accuse the army of killing numerous civilians in Gaza with the use of AI-powered targeting systems. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Jerusalem, Noga Tarnopolsky.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f9ad5328-c62d-11f1-ac7e-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-100856-101124-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f9ad5328-c62d-11f1-ac7e-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-100856-101124-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ff72ecb4-c62d-11f1-9d3e-4900808bc323</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 11:17:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Saudi Arabia: Riyadh airport struck again by Yemen's Houthis</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/saudi-arabia-riyadh-airport-struck-again-by-yemen-s-houthis</link><description>
A new attack hit Riyadh's international airport on Sunday, a day after another attack on the airport killed at least 12 people and injured over 300. This was the deadliest on Saudi soil in over a decade. Fighting between the Iran-backed Houthis and Saudi-backed Yemeni government forces have been escalating for several weeks. Story by Juliette Brown and Caitlin Brown.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/234f8a80-c61e-11f1-bf35-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-11T224410Z-1659588386-RC241OAGCJLV-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-AIRPORT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/234f8a80-c61e-11f1-bf35-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-11T224410Z-1659588386-RC241OAGCJLV-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-AIRPORT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b709347a-c61d-11f1-bb18-637269ba2545</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 09:21:12 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Riyadh airport to remain closed after deadly Houthi attacks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261012-live-saudi-arabia-extends-suspension-of-operations-at-riyadh-airport-after-deadly-houthi-attacks</link><description>
Saudi Arabia's civil aviation body extended the suspension of operations at Riyadh's international airport Monday following a series of deadly attacks by Yemen's Iran-aligned Houthi rebels over the weekend. The statement announcing the decision did not specify when operations would resume. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c294b8ba-c5ae-11f1-9976-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-11T133451Z-158209492-RC211OAHP5D3-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-AIRPORT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c294b8ba-c5ae-11f1-9976-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-11T133451Z-158209492-RC211OAHP5D3-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-AIRPORT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c7ce9790-c5d3-11f1-b586-fb36e88e0e35</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 08:41:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c294b8ba-c5ae-11f1-9976-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-11T133451Z-158209492-RC211OAHP5D3-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-AIRPORT.jpg">© Social Media via Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Fresh Houthi strike hits Riyadh airport a day after deadly attack</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261012-houthi-strike-riyadh-airport-yemen</link><description>
A fresh Houthi strike hit Riyadh’s King Khalid International Airport on Sunday, killing a Pakistani resident and wounding 11, Saudi authorities said. The attack followed a strike that killed at least 12 people and halted airport operations on Saturday. The Iran-backed group threatened further attacks on Saudi Arabia’s transit hubs.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c294b8ba-c5ae-11f1-9976-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-11T133451Z-158209492-RC211OAHP5D3-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-AIRPORT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c294b8ba-c5ae-11f1-9976-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-11T133451Z-158209492-RC211OAHP5D3-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-AIRPORT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">adc8ce1e-c5cf-11f1-a257-89d8aea9124d</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 01:01:39 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c294b8ba-c5ae-11f1-9976-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-11T133451Z-158209492-RC211OAHP5D3-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-AIRPORT.jpg">© Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Escalating fighting in Yemen worsens food security crisis</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/escalating-fighting-in-yemen-worsens-food-security-crisis</link><description>
Aid agencies in Yemen highlighted the growing hunger emergency sparked by renewed fighting between Houthi opposition forces and Government troops, after mobile health clinics reported that hundreds of children displaced by the violence are suffering from the most deadly form of malnutrition.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4ec9538a-c53d-11f1-afd5-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261011-080348-080521-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4ec9538a-c53d-11f1-afd5-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261011-080348-080521-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">534db6e4-c53d-11f1-ad6d-15d0d6d37d45</guid><pubDate>Sun, 11 Oct 2026 06:34:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Saudi Arabia threatens 'decisive' response after Riyadh airport strike kills at least 12</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261011-riyadh-airport-strike-kills-12-saudi-arabia-threatens-decisive-response</link><description>
Saudi Arabia vowed to retaliate against Yemen’s Houthi rebels on Sunday after a strike on Riyadh’s international airport killed a dozen people and wounded more than 300, marking the kingdom's deadliest strike in a decade.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5c423ba-b42e-11f1-9171-6f779f079bc8/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-19T114800Z-1100229945-RC28MNAOL58F-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-YEMEN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5c423ba-b42e-11f1-9171-6f779f079bc8/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-19T114800Z-1100229945-RC28MNAOL58F-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-YEMEN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7e70621c-c539-11f1-b6fc-57b5bb5be337</guid><pubDate>Sun, 11 Oct 2026 06:21:50 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5c423ba-b42e-11f1-9171-6f779f079bc8/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-19T114800Z-1100229945-RC28MNAOL58F-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-YEMEN.jpg">© Stringer, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Riyadh airport strike kills 12, Saudi Arabia threatens 'decisive' response</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261011-at-least-twelve-killed-multiple-people-wounded-in-attack-on-riyadh-airport-1</link><description>
Saudi Arabia vowed to retaliate against Yemen’s Houthi rebels on Sunday after a strike on Riyadh’s international airport killed a dozen people and wounded more than 300, marking the kingdom's deadliest strike in a decade.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6a8b286a-c532-11f1-b166-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261011-060136-060302-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6a8b286a-c532-11f1-b166-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261011-060136-060302-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6ff26e8a-c532-11f1-9d4b-b30d91264429</guid><pubDate>Sun, 11 Oct 2026 05:16:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Houthi rebels claim latest attacks on Riyadh airport, following Saturday's deadly strike</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261011-live-saudi-arabia-vows-decisive-response-after-deadly-houthi-strike-on-riyadh-airport</link><description>
Yemen's Houthis have claimed responsibility for attacks on Riyadh's international airport on Sunday, which the Saudi Civil Aviation Authority reported as having caused injuries. The attacks follow Saturday’s strike on the civilian airport which killed at least 12, constituting the deadliest on Saudi soil in more than a decade. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0521e248-c550-11f1-8562-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-02-17T000000Z-191424583-MT1IMGOST000OXOJ1D-RTRMADP-3-IMAGO-IMAGES.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0521e248-c550-11f1-8562-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-02-17T000000Z-191424583-MT1IMGOST000OXOJ1D-RTRMADP-3-IMAGO-IMAGES.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a64eb6c0-c530-11f1-814f-61908b950495</guid><pubDate>Sun, 11 Oct 2026 05:04:26 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0521e248-c550-11f1-8562-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-02-17T000000Z-191424583-MT1IMGOST000OXOJ1D-RTRMADP-3-IMAGO-IMAGES.jpg">© Markus Mainka, Imago via Reuters</source><dc:creator>Anaëlle JONAH</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Why Yemen's war is escalating</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261010-spotlight</link><description>
Loud explosions have been heard at Riyadh airport. Diplomatic sources say that Yemen's Houthi fighters have launched another missile attack on the international hub. At least five people have been treated for extensive injuries, according to hospital sources, with dozens more injured. The Saudi government hasn't yet commented, as more airlines cancel flights to the country. Meanwhile, Saudi jets continue to strike Yemen, in support of the Yemeni government involved in fierce fighting to push back Houthi positions.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/52ff5d46-c4d4-11f1-a7b0-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/Houthi-000-D2RW9CQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/52ff5d46-c4d4-11f1-a7b0-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/Houthi-000-D2RW9CQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0d9708a0-c4cd-11f1-9e5c-477a06fce4ea</guid><pubDate>Sat, 10 Oct 2026 18:22:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gavin LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>At least twelve killed, multiple people wounded in attack on Riyadh airport</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261010-riyadh-airport-suspends-operations-after-attack-leaves-multiple-people-wounded</link><description>
At least twelve people were killed in an attack on Riyadh's King Khalid International Airport on Saturday, including an Egyptian flight attendant, according to a medical source at a local hospital. Earlier this week, another attack on the airport by the Houthis killed three people and damaged a plane, though the Iran-backed group did not announce any new attacks on Saturday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3556cb4-c4d3-11f1-90a7-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/AP314998123886.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3556cb4-c4d3-11f1-90a7-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/AP314998123886.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0a40824c-c4ca-11f1-a6da-91b86ff72895</guid><pubDate>Sat, 10 Oct 2026 18:03:32 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3556cb4-c4d3-11f1-90a7-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/AP314998123886.jpg">© Carolyn Kaster, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
